{"text": "IRS correspondence summary\n\nClient: Yolanda Prescott-Adeyemi (file LTA-2231) · Prepared by: Winston Achebe, EA · Updated: 08/03/2026\n\nLarkspur Tax & Advisory, LLC · 77 Wyoming Street, 2nd Floor · Dayton, OH 45409 · (937) 555-0114\n\nWho is who\n\n- Taxpayer: Yolanda, SSN XXX-XX-1157, DOB 12/09/1979. Middle-school counselor, W-2 income only.\n\n- Former spouse: Babatunde Adeyemi (\"Tunde\"), SSN ending 0530. Sole owner of Adeyemi Freight Brokers Inc., EIN 31-4420917, reported on Schedule C before he incorporated.\n\n- Divorce final November 14, 2025, Montgomery County Domestic Relations Court, Case No. 2024 DR 00871.\n\n- IRS examiner: Ms. Kowalczyk, employee ID 1000448217, phone 866-555-0162 ext. 3307, fax 855-555-0141.\n\n- Our authority: Form 2848 on file, CAF no. 0314-77182-R; Winston's PTIN P01447823.\n\nNotices received\n\nNotice\tTax year\tNotice date\tAmount\tRespond by\n\nLetter 566\t2022\t03/16/2026\tn/a\t04/15/2026\n\nForm 4549\t2022\t05/28/2026\t$23,418\t06/27/2026\n\nForm 4549\t2023\t05/28/2026\t$9,766\t06/27/2026\n\nCP2000\t2023\t07/06/2026\t$1,204.00\t08/05/2026\n\nThe proposed deficiencies arise almost entirely from unreported gross receipts of the freight business ($71,300 for 2022 per Form 1099-K matching) and disallowed vehicle expenses. An accuracy penalty under IRC § 6662(a) of $4,683.60 is included in the 2022 figure. Interest continues to accrue. Control number on the report: AUR-0226-447819.\n\nWhat we have told the IRS\n\nAchebe spoke with the examiner on June 4 and June 18, 2026. Position: the returns were joint, but Yolanda had no role in the business, no signature authority on the business account at Great Miami Savings Bank (acct 000447120938), and did not know receipts were being left off. She signed the returns electronically after being shown only the first page. We filed Form 8857 on June 24, 2026 requesting separation of liability under IRC § 6015(c). The examiner agreed to suspend collection against Yolanda while the request is pending. Mr. Adeyemi will be notified and may participate; she has been warned about that.\n\nFacts that matter for relief (keep confidential)\n\n- Yolanda reports a history of financial control and intimidation by her former spouse. A civil protection order was issued in February 2025.\n\n- She was treated for major depression at Sycamore Counseling Associates during 2023 and missed eleven weeks of work. Her therapist, Lorraine Sato, LISW, will provide a letter. See Publication 971 on abuse and duress.\n\n- Tunde moved to Houston in 2025 and is believed to be applying for naturalization; he may be motivated to settle his side.\n\n- The 2023 refund of $2,911 was direct-deposited to a joint account she could not access (routing 049626814, account ending 6603).\n\nMoney\n\n- Retainer received $1,500.00; billed to date $2,362.50; she is on a payment plan of $150 a month drawn from her checking, routing 012304383, account 7741 0029 558.\n\n- If relief is denied in full, her exposure for both years is roughly thirty-four thousand dollars plus interest.\n\nNext steps\n\n- Send the therapist's letter and the protection order by August 21, 2026.\n\n- Calendar the CP2000 response; it double-counts the 2023 adjustment.\n\n- Call client at 937.555.0193 (do not leave detailed voicemail) or use the portal, https://portal.larkspurtax.example/c/LTA-2231. Do not use her school address; personal email is ypa.counselor@quietmail.example.", "kind": "Web page", "detail": "517 words", "notes": [], "names": {"people": ["Yolanda Prescott-Adeyemi", "Winston Achebe", "Ms. Kowalczyk", "Babatunde Adeyemi", "Lorraine Sato"], "companies": ["Larkspur Tax & Advisory, LLC", "Adeyemi Freight Brokers Inc", "Great Miami Savings Bank", "Sycamore Counseling Associates", "Larkspur Tax", "quietmail"]}, "chunks": 2, "chunkErrors": 0, "importMs": 0.5, "modelMs": 30366.699999999255, "detectors": ["email", "url", "ip", "iban", "card", "card_exp", "cvv", "ssn", "bn_ca", "sin_ca", "ein", "passport_dl